1
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:17,520
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
I kicked a pebble and
even my shoes went flying.

3
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:32,920
onto the head of the carpenter
I'd been putting in a choke hold,

4
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:39,120
they laughed at me for still being a brat.

5
00:00:39,780 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I somehow stir up some energy,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:46,100
Pachinko Kameari

7
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:49,300
not even a yawn changes anything.

8
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:53,160
The streets are strangely kind.

9
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,140
From the pointed hat's water spout,

10
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:07,440
with vast nature, the sunset falls.

11
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:15,900
Tomorrow too,
it'll end just like this, won't it?

12
00:01:15,900 --> 00:01:19,740
Katsushika Shibamata, happiness too.

13
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:22,440
Only after losing it did I realize.

14
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:24,680
Because I'm such a fool.

15
00:01:50,520 --> 00:01:52,900
Sorry, this is the wrong house.

16
00:01:52,900 --> 00:02:05,740
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeh!

17
00:02:05,740 --> 00:02:07,400
You're interrupting me while I'm working,
damn it.

18
00:02:08,080 --> 00:02:10,140
Sorry, my hand slipped.

19
00:02:10,140 --> 00:02:12,180
Honestly, can't you even sit
and enjoy a cup of tea properly?

20
00:02:12,180 --> 00:02:14,480
That's exactly why you'll never get married.

21
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:16,400
Look around you.

22
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:19,140
Hiromi, Keiko, Kaoru,

23
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:20,980
they've all gotten married.

24
00:02:21,420 --> 00:02:22,720
Before you know it,

25
00:02:22,720 --> 00:02:24,800
Reiko will be the only one left unsold.

26
00:02:25,820 --> 00:02:26,380
What?

27
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:28,120
Stop nagging me, you're so persistent.

28
00:02:28,460 --> 00:02:30,540
And I was trying to make you tea, too.

29
00:02:30,540 --> 00:02:32,300
Well, aren't you getting cocky.

30
00:02:32,980 --> 00:02:34,460
It's not that I can't get married,

31
00:02:34,460 --> 00:02:35,480
I just haven't gone yet.

32
00:02:37,780 --> 00:02:40,580
Writing your incident reports isn't even my job,
you know.

33
00:02:40,580 --> 00:02:41,360
What was that?

34
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:44,960
Shut up!

35
00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:45,920
What?

36
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:51,140
What is it?

37
00:03:04,860 --> 00:03:06,960
Who the hell is this guy! Honestly!

38
00:03:07,460 --> 00:03:08,440
N-no way!

39
00:03:18,200 --> 00:03:19,260
Reiko-chan

40
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:22,240
Just as I thought.

41
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:27,320
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah,
yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

42
00:03:28,820 --> 00:03:30,740
President, are you all right?

43
00:03:30,740 --> 00:03:33,100
I got hit really hard.

44
00:03:33,820 --> 00:03:35,020
Daddy, honestly.

45
00:03:35,020 --> 00:03:37,100
Daddy, no way.

46
00:03:37,440 --> 00:03:38,860
He's Reiko's dad.

47
00:03:38,860 --> 00:03:42,360
I can't believe that guy is
the president of a major company.

48
00:03:43,060 --> 00:03:44,340
Papa, are you okay?

49
00:03:44,340 --> 00:03:44,580
Are you all right?

50
00:03:44,760 --> 00:03:46,400
Reiko!

51
00:03:47,860 --> 00:03:49,280
What's the sudden visit for?

52
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:53,140
You never answer when I call, so I
stopped by while I was on a business trip.

53
00:03:54,780 --> 00:03:56,795
This police box is a filthy place, isn't it?

54
00:03:56,845 --> 00:03:59,500
You can't get any work done like this.

55
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:02,180
The mess is your fault, you know.

56
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:04,004
If I were the one in charge,

57
00:04:04,054 --> 00:04:06,980
I'd tear it down right away
and make it a splendid office.

58
00:04:07,340 --> 00:04:10,920
When the police are privatized,
buy this police box from them.

59
00:04:12,780 --> 00:04:14,700
So this is Reiko's desk.

60
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:17,620
It's the desk of a healer.

61
00:04:17,620 --> 00:04:18,580
What a mess.

62
00:04:18,580 --> 00:04:20,220
She's really putting up with a lot.

63
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:22,340
The chair's terrible too.

64
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:25,640
What a poor kitchen.

65
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:26,640
Whoa.

66
00:04:26,640 --> 00:04:28,740
What an unsanitary toilet.

67
00:04:29,360 --> 00:04:31,700
This isn't a place fit for humans to work.

68
00:04:31,700 --> 00:04:35,340
I had no idea Reiko was
being treated this badly.

69
00:04:35,340 --> 00:04:38,500
You came all the way from
Kobe just to complain?

70
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:39,760
Right.

71
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:41,740
Hey, Takeshita!

72
00:04:42,300 --> 00:04:42,840
Yes, sir!

73
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:45,220
Operation 189, begin!

74
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:49,460
What's going on, hey!

75
00:04:50,360 --> 00:04:51,340
Come on, out you go!

76
00:04:51,420 --> 00:04:52,020
Hey, hold on!

77
00:04:52,900 --> 00:04:53,260
Hey!

78
00:04:53,540 --> 00:04:54,120
Hey, Papa!

79
00:04:54,380 --> 00:04:57,520
Papa's keeping watch here, so go on,
get out there and do some patrolling!

80
00:04:58,700 --> 00:05:00,640
Papa, open up!

81
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:02,360
Hey, I said open up!

82
00:05:02,900 --> 00:05:04,220
Papa...

83
00:05:04,220 --> 00:05:06,440
What an utterly incomprehensible old man!

84
00:05:11,220 --> 00:05:11,700
Ah

85
00:05:12,980 --> 00:05:14,080
What on earth is that?

86
00:05:15,320 --> 00:05:16,340
Ryotsu

87
00:05:16,340 --> 00:05:19,540
What's this helicopter?
It's you again, isn't it?

88
00:05:19,540 --> 00:05:21,020
That's not it!

89
00:05:21,560 --> 00:05:23,000
Chief, the truth is...

90
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:26,380
Sorry to keep you waiting.

91
00:05:34,140 --> 00:05:36,320
We've got the latest office equipment.

92
00:05:36,780 --> 00:05:38,900
It's hard to believe this is a police box,
it's so luxurious.

93
00:05:39,740 --> 00:05:41,860
This desk is still the same as before.

94
00:05:41,860 --> 00:05:44,240
It's a state-of-the-art
toilet seat with heating.

95
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:46,920
Andren, it really is warm.

96
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:49,580
This is a West German-made system kitchen.

97
00:05:50,680 --> 00:05:51,660
Hey, Reiko.

98
00:05:52,960 --> 00:05:53,800
What on earth is this?

99
00:05:54,360 --> 00:05:56,200
My daughter is always in your care.

100
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:58,560
I'm Reiko's father, Pyunpyunmaru Akimoto.

101
00:05:58,940 --> 00:06:00,920
Well, how do you do?

102
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:03,040
Wow, what firepower!

103
00:06:03,660 --> 00:06:04,480
Nice.

104
00:06:04,860 --> 00:06:07,520
With this, even the water for
cup ramen will boil in an instant!

105
00:06:08,140 --> 00:06:08,920
Beautiful lady.

106
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:12,660
How about it? I renovated so
it'd be easier for Reiko to work.

107
00:06:12,660 --> 00:06:15,200
Ugh, just put everything
back the way it was!

108
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:17,000
Eh

109
00:06:18,260 --> 00:06:20,680
After I went to all that trouble
to make it comfortable for Reiko.

110
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:22,160
You're really going to put it all back?

111
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:25,180
Of course.
What did you come here for, anyway?

112
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:26,760
Right.

113
00:06:29,780 --> 00:06:32,540
Wow, that's quite a lot of omiai photos.

114
00:06:32,540 --> 00:06:36,200
They've been arriving every day from business partners and banks,
you know.

115
00:06:36,740 --> 00:06:39,000
Just look through them,
even if it's only a glance.

116
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:40,320
There sure are a lot.

117
00:06:40,320 --> 00:06:42,580
Looking through them alone would take days.

118
00:06:44,160 --> 00:06:46,320
Hey, Reiko, what about this one?

119
00:06:46,460 --> 00:06:49,480
The eldest son of some cheap conglomerate. He saw you at a party and
Translation>
(see note)

120
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:51,320
Sorry, but please turn him down, Daddy.

121
00:06:51,700 --> 00:06:53,740
I'm not planning to get married yet.

122
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:54,720
What?

123
00:06:57,460 --> 00:07:00,660
I see. Got it.

124
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:04,980
I only brought these omiai
photos because I was asked to.

125
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:07,740
Whom you choose is up to you, Reiko.
It's your life.

126
00:07:08,180 --> 00:07:09,580
I trust you.

127
00:07:09,860 --> 00:07:10,460
Papa.

128
00:07:11,020 --> 00:07:12,060
Hey, clean this up.

129
00:07:12,220 --> 00:07:12,560
Yes, sir.

130
00:07:12,860 --> 00:07:13,560
Thank goodness.

131
00:07:13,840 --> 00:07:15,380
He's a reasonable old man, isn't he?

132
00:07:15,840 --> 00:07:16,440
Well, yeah.

133
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:18,800
So, Reiko, just this one favor, please.

134
00:07:19,940 --> 00:07:21,800
It's the son from Daikin Real Estate.

135
00:07:22,380 --> 00:07:24,880
We've had a long relationship
with Daikin Real Estate,

136
00:07:26,200 --> 00:07:27,200
so I can't just turn them down.

137
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:29,440
Could you at least meet him?

138
00:07:29,440 --> 00:07:29,900
But...

139
00:07:30,320 --> 00:07:32,600
President, it's almost time for the meeting.

140
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:33,700
Right.

141
00:07:33,700 --> 00:07:34,580
Papa.

142
00:07:35,780 --> 00:07:36,480
I'm counting on you.

143
00:07:38,280 --> 00:07:39,760
Papa, honestly.

144
00:07:40,540 --> 00:07:43,540
the 32-year-old only
son of Daikin Real Estate,

145
00:07:43,540 --> 00:07:45,400
with a 2,000-tsubo home in Ashiya.

146
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:47,960
A shriveled cucumber of a guy like this,
you know.

147
00:07:48,740 --> 00:07:51,300
A company with 70 billion yen in annual sales,
a top-tier company.

148
00:07:51,900 --> 00:07:53,060
Well, it can't be helped.

149
00:07:53,060 --> 00:07:55,180
Let's meet him and turn him down.

150
00:07:56,580 --> 00:07:58,780
What a waste of 70 billion yen!

151
00:07:58,780 --> 00:08:00,800
It's not about the money, is it?

152
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:03,840
But if he really takes a liking to Reiko...

153
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:06,660
then turning him down
would be even worse, right?

154
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:10,060
Yes, it might actually turn out to be rude,
you know.

155
00:08:10,060 --> 00:08:13,600
What should I do? This is a problem.

156
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:14,680
Don't worry, don't worry.

157
00:08:14,680 --> 00:08:17,520
If Reiko goes to the
meeting in her usual way,

158
00:08:17,520 --> 00:08:20,560
the other side will be scared
off and turn it down themselves.

159
00:08:21,040 --> 00:08:23,040
Hey, Ryo-chan, what do you mean by that?

160
00:08:24,520 --> 00:08:27,460
If you don't knock it off,
I'll knock you flat, Ryo-chan.

161
00:08:28,460 --> 00:08:31,047
If you anger this divinely possessed Reiko,

162
00:08:31,097 --> 00:08:33,580
I'll fold you up and toss
you into the Sumida River.

163
00:08:34,080 --> 00:08:35,400
Honestly, Ryo-chan.

164
00:08:35,740 --> 00:08:37,200
Honestly, Ryo-chan.

165
00:08:38,400 --> 00:08:40,320
When did I ever do such a thing?

166
00:08:41,580 --> 00:08:42,300
That's it!

167
00:08:47,540 --> 00:08:48,600
Reiko-san.

168
00:08:54,800 --> 00:08:57,360
The Akimotos seem to be running late,
don't they?

169
00:08:57,360 --> 00:09:01,260
Yes, they're already more than an hour late.

170
00:09:02,140 --> 00:09:04,040
Dear, I need to pee.

171
00:09:04,040 --> 00:09:07,720
Hold it in.
And Kazuo, you understand, don't you?

172
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:10,800
Whatever it takes,
you have to close this engagement.

173
00:09:11,220 --> 00:09:14,700
The Akimotos are a zaibatsu on a
completely different scale from us.

174
00:09:14,700 --> 00:09:18,960
Their assets may one day be yours, you know.

175
00:09:18,960 --> 00:09:21,230
Now, listen!
If she has a bad temper or something,

176
00:09:21,280 --> 00:09:24,220
you must turn a blind eye to a few flaws!

177
00:09:24,380 --> 00:09:25,760
Got it, Mom.

178
00:09:26,020 --> 00:09:28,360
Hey, sorry I'm late. Hello, hello.

179
00:09:28,460 --> 00:09:29,600
Looks like you've arrived.

180
00:09:30,700 --> 00:09:32,816
Reiko's father has caught a cold,

181
00:09:32,866 --> 00:09:35,440
so I, her uncle, came in his place.
Nice to meet you.

182
00:09:38,740 --> 00:09:40,560
I'm Reiko. Nice to meet you.

183
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:53,060
It's totally different from the photo, Mom.

184
00:09:54,300 --> 00:09:56,460
That means the engagement is definitely off.

185
00:09:56,460 --> 00:09:58,620
If it succeeds,
the Tsurukame Prefecture katsudon is yours.

186
00:09:59,160 --> 00:10:01,240
Are you Reiko-san?

187
00:10:01,980 --> 00:10:04,500
Yes, I'm Reiko. Do you have some questions?

188
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:08,480
Well you seem a little different
from your arranged-marriage photo.

189
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:13,520
I get told that a lot.
I just photograph badly.

190
00:10:14,120 --> 00:10:17,200
Reiko-san,
your voice is quite husky, isn't it?

191
00:10:18,960 --> 00:10:21,952
Five hundred a day,
plus drinking too much shochu and beer.

192
00:10:22,002 --> 00:10:24,740
and from karaoke,
my voice ended up like this.

193
00:10:24,940 --> 00:10:26,667
Uh, Reiko-san is...

194
00:10:26,717 --> 00:10:29,680
I hear you have a wide range of hobbies.
You ride horses too, don't you?

195
00:10:29,940 --> 00:10:32,193
I love horses. Especially horse racing.

196
00:10:32,243 --> 00:10:34,053
And then there's keirin, mahjong,

197
00:10:34,103 --> 00:10:38,100
pachinko, hanafuda, karate,
boxing, and I love fighting too.

198
00:10:38,160 --> 00:10:39,779
Brawling is the best of all.

199
00:10:39,829 --> 00:10:43,320
Everyone ends up covered in blood,
and wahhhhh.

200
00:10:43,820 --> 00:10:45,840
Reiko-san is so good at jokes.

201
00:10:45,840 --> 00:10:48,060
I'm serious.

202
00:10:48,060 --> 00:10:50,860
Or shall I demonstrate right here?

203
00:10:50,860 --> 00:10:51,660
Hey!

204
00:10:52,440 --> 00:10:55,500
If Reiko's reputation gets damaged later on,
that would be bad.

205
00:10:55,500 --> 00:10:56,920
Go all out.

206
00:10:56,920 --> 00:10:59,980
The goal is to get the other side
to turn down the meeting, right?

207
00:10:59,980 --> 00:11:02,140
We need to leave nothing to chance.

208
00:11:02,140 --> 00:11:04,260
She's quite the lively young lady.

209
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:07,500
She's been raised to be very free-spirited.

210
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:09,880
Mama Reiko is scary, you know.

211
00:11:09,880 --> 00:11:10,940
I told you.

212
00:11:10,940 --> 00:11:13,460
You'll have to overlook a few of her flaws.

213
00:11:13,460 --> 00:11:14,000
A few.

214
00:11:15,840 --> 00:11:19,020
I got into a huge fight with the other side,
and it was really fun.

215
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:21,140
Ryo-chan.

216
00:11:34,720 --> 00:11:35,435
Wow,

217
00:11:35,485 --> 00:11:39,120
what a splendid drinking style you have,
Kazuo-san.

218
00:11:39,120 --> 00:11:41,000
Yes, it's splendid.

219
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:44,600
That's nice.
I've grown quite fond of your bold manner.

220
00:11:44,600 --> 00:11:46,843
Damn, then...

221
00:11:46,893 --> 00:11:48,900
That looks delicious.

222
00:11:56,440 --> 00:11:57,480
Delicious.

223
00:11:57,480 --> 00:11:58,760
Reiko's so happy.

224
00:11:58,760 --> 00:12:01,080
I can't hold back anymore.

225
00:12:03,580 --> 00:12:05,220
I'm stuffed.

226
00:12:05,220 --> 00:12:08,380
What a vivid way you eat, Kazuo-san.

227
00:12:08,980 --> 00:12:10,700
It's a vivid way of eating.

228
00:12:10,700 --> 00:12:13,700
After all, health comes first, doesn't it.

229
00:12:13,700 --> 00:12:16,220
I like you even more now.

230
00:12:16,840 --> 00:12:19,040
This one's tougher than I thought.

231
00:12:19,900 --> 00:12:22,520
Well, what can you do.

232
00:12:23,500 --> 00:12:26,460
Well then,
time to leave the young ones to it.

233
00:12:28,700 --> 00:12:30,240
Kazuo-san, let's go.

234
00:12:30,660 --> 00:12:31,600
Mom, she's scary.

235
00:12:31,780 --> 00:12:33,020
Hurry up and get over here, you bastard.

236
00:12:34,200 --> 00:12:36,200
Well then, Grandpa,
we're going to go a bit further.

237
00:12:36,900 --> 00:12:38,580
Have a nice, long time.

238
00:12:38,720 --> 00:12:39,040
Mom!

239
00:12:39,820 --> 00:12:41,280
Good luck, Kazuo-san!

240
00:12:41,480 --> 00:12:42,080
Mom!

241
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:45,360
Now, I'm going to give you a good time.

242
00:12:59,240 --> 00:12:59,640
Why?

243
00:13:03,440 --> 00:13:05,100
Mom's not here anymore, you know.

244
00:13:05,180 --> 00:13:06,880
Kazuo and me, all alone.

245
00:13:12,380 --> 00:13:15,200
I thought we'd settle
things at the restaurant.

246
00:13:15,740 --> 00:13:16,674
Poor thing.

247
00:13:16,724 --> 00:13:19,960
If he'd just turned her down early,
he wouldn't have to suffer any more.

248
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:21,900
Well, what should we play?

249
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:25,000
This is me?

250
00:13:25,360 --> 00:13:26,880
Even I find it creepy.

251
00:13:27,100 --> 00:13:28,680
It doesn't even look human.

252
00:13:29,240 --> 00:13:30,200
Hey, look at that.

253
00:13:30,700 --> 00:13:31,820
What an ugly hag.

254
00:13:31,980 --> 00:13:33,560
How does she even walk
the streets like that?

255
00:13:33,700 --> 00:13:35,300
That one's really human, you know.

256
00:13:35,580 --> 00:13:38,200
A-ah, hold on a sec.

257
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:40,440
A gorilla would look better.

258
00:13:41,540 --> 00:13:43,300
Who's ugly, you bastard?

259
00:13:43,700 --> 00:13:46,040
I'm not taking that crap from you lot.

260
00:13:46,660 --> 00:13:48,580
Mind your own damn business, bastard.

261
00:13:48,820 --> 00:13:49,760
S-sorry.

262
00:13:50,740 --> 00:13:52,100
Sorry to keep you waiting.

263
00:13:52,320 --> 00:13:54,626
N-no, it's just that Reiko-san...

264
00:13:54,676 --> 00:13:58,120
you're quite the fiery type, aren't you.

265
00:13:59,680 --> 00:14:04,120
Is that so? When someone says something nasty about me,
I just can't help but lash out.

266
00:14:06,880 --> 00:14:10,340
About that classical concert Mom gave me...

267
00:14:10,340 --> 00:14:11,400
Classical.

268
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:15,620
Andre Heilrichten Johann Autobahn-style.

269
00:14:15,620 --> 00:14:20,880
Humbert Underdgen Public Work No.
348, Song of the Hetanchō Forest.

270
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:24,060
apparently the performance runs six hours,

271
00:14:25,040 --> 00:14:29,240
but I'm sorry, I absolutely hate classical music,
so let's do it another time.

272
00:14:29,900 --> 00:14:32,560
Looks like we don't share the same tastes.
What should we do?

273
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:36,280
If you don't like it, feel free to turn it down.
The arranged meeting, too.

274
00:14:36,280 --> 00:14:37,340
I see.

275
00:14:37,340 --> 00:14:41,360
Don't worry about it.
We'll chalk it up to fate and give up.

276
00:14:41,900 --> 00:14:44,040
Well then, I'm sorry, but

277
00:14:44,040 --> 00:14:44,460
Mm.

278
00:14:44,460 --> 00:14:45,500
about this matter...

279
00:14:45,500 --> 00:14:46,420
Mm-hmm.

280
00:14:47,280 --> 00:14:48,160
Excuse me.

281
00:14:49,140 --> 00:14:50,440
Yes, Mom.

282
00:14:51,040 --> 00:14:53,460
Kazuo-san,
good luck with the arranged meeting!

283
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:55,640
You have to win her over no matter what!

284
00:14:56,800 --> 00:14:59,180
Yeah, I know, Mom.

285
00:15:00,160 --> 00:15:04,240
Kazuo and I are getting along just fine,
so don't worry.

286
00:15:04,660 --> 00:15:06,160
Hello? Hello?

287
00:15:06,160 --> 00:15:10,780
Sorry, my hand slipped.

288
00:15:11,620 --> 00:15:13,520
Hello? Hello, Kazuo-san?

289
00:15:15,020 --> 00:15:15,820
So, yes?

290
00:15:16,360 --> 00:15:18,140
About refusing the arranged meeting...

291
00:15:18,140 --> 00:15:21,220
N-no, refusing? Not at all!

292
00:15:21,740 --> 00:15:22,560
I see.

293
00:15:24,060 --> 00:15:27,080
This "prize woman" plan isn't getting anywhere.
Now it's time for the next move.

294
00:15:27,520 --> 00:15:30,780
I want something. Will you buy it for me?

295
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:32,140
Of course, sure thing.

296
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:37,080
480,000 yen?

297
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:40,820
What a lovely bag.

298
00:15:41,720 --> 00:15:42,440
This one?

299
00:15:43,060 --> 00:15:44,660
Yes, he's scared, he's scared.

300
00:15:45,660 --> 00:15:47,920
No, I want it, I want it, Kazuo-san.

301
00:15:48,420 --> 00:15:50,700
Yes, good taste. Understood.

302
00:15:50,700 --> 00:15:51,771
Hey, wait,

303
00:15:51,821 --> 00:15:54,948
Didn't that guy get a digit wrong?

304
00:15:54,998 --> 00:15:56,120
It's 480,000, you know.

305
00:15:57,120 --> 00:15:59,060
Here you go, Reiko-san. Please.

306
00:15:59,200 --> 00:16:00,480
Thank you.

307
00:16:01,700 --> 00:16:04,118
He paid 480,000 yen for this junk.

308
00:16:04,168 --> 00:16:06,500
Good, enjoy your showing
off while you still can.

309
00:16:07,160 --> 00:16:09,340
Reiko, I want jewelry too.

310
00:16:09,500 --> 00:16:10,320
Jewelry

311
00:16:10,560 --> 00:16:11,800
I want it, I want it.

312
00:16:19,240 --> 00:16:21,300
Such a terrifying price for a mere pebble.

313
00:16:21,300 --> 00:16:23,020
I can't understand
people who buy this stuff.

314
00:16:23,020 --> 00:16:25,560
Please, choose whichever one you like.

315
00:16:26,440 --> 00:16:28,760
Can I really pick whichever one I want?

316
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:29,600
Yes.

317
00:16:30,080 --> 00:16:31,880
This big one...

318
00:16:31,880 --> 00:16:34,000
the one for 1.2 million yen.

319
00:16:34,440 --> 00:16:34,840
Yes.

320
00:16:37,460 --> 00:16:38,260
Damn it!

321
00:16:38,720 --> 00:16:39,440
Just you watch.

322
00:16:39,440 --> 00:16:42,000
Ugh, I'll buy so much my eyeballs
pop out and I still can't pay for it!

323
00:16:42,280 --> 00:16:45,023
This red one, and the green one next to it,

324
00:16:45,073 --> 00:16:48,360
this big one. Excuse me for a moment.

325
00:16:48,440 --> 00:16:49,140
No, that won't do.

326
00:16:49,500 --> 00:16:51,160
This one, this one, and this one too.

327
00:16:51,220 --> 00:16:51,600
Madam.

328
00:16:51,960 --> 00:16:53,560
No matter how beautiful the other person is,

329
00:16:53,610 --> 00:16:57,360
being that brazen at a first meeting
would make me lose all interest.

330
00:16:57,780 --> 00:16:59,440
Well, I suppose the plan was a success.

331
00:17:02,620 --> 00:17:04,860
Could you wrap up all of these?

332
00:17:05,500 --> 00:17:06,220
All of them?

333
00:17:06,940 --> 00:17:07,660
Yes, all of them.

334
00:17:09,440 --> 00:17:11,660
That comes to about 58 million yen.

335
00:17:12,050 --> 00:17:13,760
W-what, 100 million!?

336
00:17:21,420 --> 00:17:22,380
Th-that's, that's

337
00:17:22,430 --> 00:17:25,460
It's 158 million yen, apparently.

338
00:17:26,260 --> 00:17:27,760
158 million...

339
00:17:32,310 --> 00:17:32,580
Yes?

340
00:17:33,170 --> 00:17:34,540
Is a check all right?

341
00:17:34,860 --> 00:17:35,320
Ugh!

342
00:17:35,540 --> 00:17:38,640
You! How do you have so much money?!

343
00:17:39,440 --> 00:17:42,200
My dad gave me a company last year.

344
00:17:42,200 --> 00:17:44,360
I'm the president of it, so...

345
00:17:44,800 --> 00:17:45,940
Is that right?

346
00:17:47,940 --> 00:17:50,540
I may not have courage or strength,

347
00:17:50,540 --> 00:17:53,200
but I have more money than most people.

348
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:55,480
Rest assured, Reiko-san.

349
00:17:55,960 --> 00:17:58,320
I'd sell my soul for
just one bowl of katsudon.

350
00:17:58,320 --> 00:17:59,780
Right, the next plan.

351
00:18:02,220 --> 00:18:03,240
That was a mistake.

352
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:04,480
I can't believe it.

353
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:07,180
Looks like it's finally our turn.

354
00:18:07,180 --> 00:18:12,960
Hey, is there anything else you want?
No, that's plenty, thank you.

355
00:18:13,840 --> 00:18:19,400
Even that guy's a loser,
but it's a miracle that she has a man at all

356
00:18:24,100 --> 00:18:25,480
Yone-san!

357
00:18:25,480 --> 00:18:26,320
Me

358
00:18:26,320 --> 00:18:29,620
If it isn't Kei-chan.

359
00:18:31,420 --> 00:18:32,140
It's sour.

360
00:18:32,140 --> 00:18:35,120
Bear with it.
I'll share some tsukudani with you later.

361
00:18:35,680 --> 00:18:37,840
Reiko, is he a friend of yours?

362
00:18:38,040 --> 00:18:40,280
He's my ex-boyfriend.
He's handsome, isn't he?

363
00:18:40,720 --> 00:18:41,780
No way!

364
00:18:42,740 --> 00:18:45,660
Reiko-chan,
you're still as charming as ever.

365
00:18:45,880 --> 00:18:49,860
Oh no, it'd be a real problem if
old flames started blazing again.

366
00:18:52,580 --> 00:18:54,760
Hey, Reiko. I've missed you.

367
00:18:56,320 --> 00:18:58,440
It's Honda-kun, my ex before the ex.

368
00:18:58,440 --> 00:18:59,460
Ex before the ex?

369
00:18:59,620 --> 00:19:02,380
Reiko-san, come with me in my car.

370
00:19:05,480 --> 00:19:08,060
We're doing this for your sake, you know.

371
00:19:08,540 --> 00:19:13,520
Why don't we take my car out toward Haneda?

372
00:19:13,800 --> 00:19:17,420
No, let's speed down the Daisan
Keihin in my car to Yokohama.

373
00:19:17,420 --> 00:19:21,600
Sorry, I'm in the middle of an arranged meeting right now,
so let's hang out another time.

374
00:19:22,200 --> 00:19:23,580
Well then, see you, Reiko.

375
00:19:23,580 --> 00:19:25,240
I love you, Reiko.

376
00:19:28,300 --> 00:19:29,000
Bye-bye.

377
00:19:30,320 --> 00:19:31,640
I can't believe it.

378
00:19:32,420 --> 00:19:33,480
What a nuisance.

379
00:19:33,480 --> 00:19:37,140
I'm so popular,
I don't have enough bodies to go around.

380
00:19:38,040 --> 00:19:39,820
Well? That's enough to make you sick of me,
isn't it?

381
00:19:41,820 --> 00:19:44,880
Well, no wonder,
having lived abroad for so long,

382
00:19:44,880 --> 00:19:46,660
Reiko is so sociable, isn't she.

383
00:19:47,600 --> 00:19:50,160
She's truly fit to be a
company president's wife.

384
00:19:50,160 --> 00:19:52,000
Ohohohohohoho.

385
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:54,920
I'm shy and have few friends,

386
00:19:56,320 --> 00:19:56,540
so it's fine.

387
00:19:58,240 --> 00:19:59,740
That was painful.

388
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:02,660
The "Go-go Cheating Woman" plan has failed.

389
00:20:03,600 --> 00:20:05,860
So this is our final plan, then.

390
00:20:07,960 --> 00:20:09,740
Good luck, Terai-senpai.

391
00:20:10,140 --> 00:20:13,980
I'm not in the mood.

392
00:20:14,980 --> 00:20:17,220
The senior officers will be here shortly.

393
00:20:17,720 --> 00:20:18,400
So,

394
00:20:19,380 --> 00:20:20,960
Hey, you there, pal.

395
00:20:20,960 --> 00:20:21,895
Help!

396
00:20:21,945 --> 00:20:25,100
Well, unreliable man, nice... goodbye.

397
00:20:26,320 --> 00:20:27,700
This gives us an excuse to refuse him.

398
00:20:28,780 --> 00:20:30,120
It's a shame for him, though.

399
00:20:30,780 --> 00:20:33,700
This time we're the ones turning him down,
so it's a sure thing.

400
00:20:34,680 --> 00:20:35,540
This way!

401
00:20:36,020 --> 00:20:39,160
Where are you going, Yone-san?
It's a nice place, a really nice place.

402
00:20:39,160 --> 00:20:40,960
That's strange. Terai and the others...

403
00:20:40,960 --> 00:20:42,960
They should be standing
by somewhere around here.

404
00:20:46,200 --> 00:20:48,020
They're late, Ryo-chan and the others.

405
00:20:48,860 --> 00:20:50,280
Where could they have gone?

406
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:53,900
I've never walked through
a place like this before.

407
00:20:54,900 --> 00:20:57,460
Hey, buddy. Where are you looking?

408
00:20:57,600 --> 00:20:59,440
So you were there all along

409
00:21:00,080 --> 00:21:02,120
Who do you think we are?

410
00:21:02,520 --> 00:21:03,320
Whoa, the real deal.

411
00:21:03,620 --> 00:21:05,620
Neko-san, help me!

412
00:21:07,860 --> 00:21:09,760
Meow~, I'm scared, no way!

413
00:21:10,480 --> 00:21:13,560
It's not what we planned, but this way
I can turn him down, so I guess it's fine.

414
00:21:15,120 --> 00:21:18,160
Calling for help like this,
what an annoying bastard.

415
00:21:18,780 --> 00:21:19,560
You bastard.

416
00:21:19,780 --> 00:21:20,840
So what do you say, you lot?

417
00:21:21,420 --> 00:21:22,480
Come on, buddy.

418
00:21:22,840 --> 00:21:23,740
Aren't you gonna apologize?

419
00:21:24,900 --> 00:21:26,220
You guys, knock it off already.

420
00:21:27,920 --> 00:21:29,300
What the hell, you ugly bitch.

421
00:21:29,300 --> 00:21:30,720
I'll ram you, ugly bitch.

422
00:21:31,560 --> 00:21:32,360
Who, me?

423
00:21:32,360 --> 00:21:34,520
You're the ugly one, you bastard!

424
00:21:34,520 --> 00:21:35,380
Let's do it.

425
00:21:35,380 --> 00:21:36,560
Hey.

426
00:22:07,420 --> 00:22:09,940
Vulgar, a spendthrift, and a man-chaser,

427
00:22:09,940 --> 00:22:12,300
she's not fit to be your wife.

428
00:22:12,660 --> 00:22:15,320
It's fine, don't worry about it.
Turn her down without hesitation.

429
00:22:15,320 --> 00:22:16,280
Reiko-san.

430
00:22:17,040 --> 00:22:17,400
Yes?

431
00:22:18,600 --> 00:22:20,380
Please marry me.

432
00:22:21,420 --> 00:22:23,900
Reiko-san, you're the ideal woman for me.

433
00:22:25,240 --> 00:22:27,440
At first, I was a little scared of you,

434
00:22:27,440 --> 00:22:29,180
but you're strong and dependable,

435
00:22:29,180 --> 00:22:32,560
you have taste for the finest things, and you're sociable.
You're perfect.

436
00:22:33,180 --> 00:22:35,840
I can't imagine any other woman but you now.

437
00:22:37,680 --> 00:22:38,480
Reiko-san!

438
00:22:42,560 --> 00:22:45,540
Has your father said anything since then?

439
00:22:45,960 --> 00:22:47,120
No, nothing at all.

440
00:22:47,120 --> 00:22:50,140
So the arranged meeting was
successfully called off, then.

441
00:22:50,560 --> 00:22:52,420
Though it does feel like
a bit of a waste somehow.

442
00:22:52,840 --> 00:22:54,540
It's thanks to everyone's cooperation.

443
00:22:55,060 --> 00:22:56,760
Especially you, Ryo-chan, thank you.

444
00:22:57,580 --> 00:22:57,980
No.

445
00:23:01,720 --> 00:23:05,760
Congratulations, Reiko!

446
00:23:06,140 --> 00:23:08,140
I hear you're engaged to Kazuo,
is that right?

447
00:23:10,800 --> 00:23:11,740
Reiko!

448
00:23:12,520 --> 00:23:12,880
No way!

449
00:23:13,460 --> 00:23:14,300
What does that mean?

450
00:23:14,720 --> 00:23:15,900
Ryotsu! Ryotsu!

451
00:23:16,580 --> 00:23:18,440
Kazuo-san, it's Reiko!

452
00:23:19,960 --> 00:23:21,000
Reiko!

453
00:23:21,620 --> 00:23:22,800
Reiko!

454
00:23:24,180 --> 00:23:24,824
Reiko,

455
00:23:24,874 --> 00:23:28,580
let's go buy that promised full-scale
remote-control helicopter today.

456
00:23:29,120 --> 00:23:30,000
I'm so happy!

457
00:23:30,120 --> 00:23:30,554
Reiko,

458
00:23:30,604 --> 00:23:34,960
I also want a Bugatti Atlantic,
that Italian luxury metal machine.

459
00:23:35,020 --> 00:23:36,220
Buy it for me, Kazuo-san.

460
00:23:36,580 --> 00:23:37,280
Fine, buddy.

461
00:23:38,280 --> 00:23:40,360
Ugh, what on earth are you thinking?!

462
00:23:40,920 --> 00:23:43,480
How long do you think this lie will work?!

463
00:23:43,780 --> 00:23:44,980
What are you talking about?

464
00:23:45,800 --> 00:23:49,360
Reiko is going to marry Kazuo
and live happily ever after.

465
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:51,300
Let's go, Kazuo-san.

466
00:23:51,540 --> 00:23:52,540
Yes, Reiko-san.

467
00:23:52,720 --> 00:23:56,600
Hey, Reiko, there's something else I want,
but anything's fine.

468
00:23:56,760 --> 00:23:57,240
Ureppi!

469
00:23:58,460 --> 00:24:00,560
Baka mooi!

470
00:24:04,520 --> 00:24:05,860
This Honda old man,

471
00:24:05,860 --> 00:24:08,520
why do I have to go all the way to Canada?

472
00:24:08,520 --> 00:24:10,660
Even so, I'm busy with work!

473
00:24:10,660 --> 00:24:13,800
Over there, the pub girls

474
00:24:13,800 --> 00:24:15,180
are all there for the picking, you say?

475
00:24:16,320 --> 00:24:17,780
Well, I suppose I could tell him.

476
00:24:17,780 --> 00:24:21,200
Say hi to the Honda
family in Canada next time.

477
00:24:30,560 --> 00:24:43,000
They say I'm a woman who can't fall in love,
but I have so many things I want to do, me.

478
00:24:44,280 --> 00:24:58,940
I want to ride a motorbike across a harsh desert,
I want to be freer than a bird.

479
00:25:00,560 --> 00:25:07,200
A lady's dreams changing at
the speed of a kaleidoscope.

480
00:25:09,180 --> 00:25:15,260
My heart's longing, sorry, wait for me.

481
00:25:15,260 --> 00:25:22,240
The dazzle of diving
into a panoramic future.

482
00:25:23,520 --> 00:25:30,100
You understand, right? Sorry, wait for me.

